{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-crankcase-start-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.42, step 7f: `process-crankcase-start`, THC, CO and NOx from START EXHAUST (102, 202, 302) and from CRANKCASE START EXHAUST (116, 216, 316) for the passenger car in Washtenaw County at the DEFAULT domain -- the DEFAULT-domain twin of `process-crankcase-start-single`. It mounts `moves-onroad.esm`, the DEFAULT domain's catalogue, exactly as `process-tirewear` does: no input database, so every domain-owned table is the default database's -- `hotellingHoursPerDay`, `startsPerDay` and the three hotelling adjustment tables EMPTY, and the input sides of `zoneRoadType`, `zone` and `hotellingActivityDistribution` mounted empty (docs/esm-conventions.md §92-§93). Nothing in the model changed for it.\n\nWHAT THE DOMAIN CHANGES. The starts are AdjustStarts.sql's other arm (`st_starts`): with no `startsPerDay` row, population x startsPerDayPerVehicle, then the age effect, the month and hour shares, the zone's startAllocFactor (the default's, the input side empty) and noOfRealDays. The county database's startsPerDay states what that arm computes, and the two oracles agree at every one of the 684 cells to the six digits MOVES writes.\n\n`n_outputRate` IS 684. `run_domainUnported` and `run_selectionUnported` are 0.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_runspecyear": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
